    "Java 25; isolated loopback offline servers with BlocksAdder and one suite-specific temporary probe, without ProtocolLib or version translation plugins.",
    "26.1.x uses minecraft-protocol 1.68.0 and minecraft-data 3.117.0 with native protocol 775.",
    "26.2/26.3 use a private bounded verification wire client with official server-generated packet-ID reports and inspected official codecs, native protocols 776/777.",
    "Official server bundle bytes were verified against Mojang version-metadata SHA-1 values before generating reports. Only private testing tools use server implementation inspection.",
    "The small wire client handles only the login/configuration and packets needed for these scenarios; it is not a full Minecraft client and does not render.",
    "Each endpoint runs 147 held/placed interaction, 56 protected timed-mining/held-break and 86 crop-view checks. Counts include public API and data assertions and are not counts of distinct native interactions."
  ],
  "fixture_corrections": [
    "Modern held entity attacks use the separate attack packet. A redundant legacy swing generated an extra left-click-air input and was removed from that test phase.",
    "26.3 teleport acknowledgement includes coordinates and angles; movement batches send client_tick_end.",
    "26.3 punch has an empty payload and replaces the former swing packet. CHANGE_DESTROY_DIRECTION inserts an action-enum entry before abort/stop; the private dig encoder maps those values.",
    "The initial 26.3 mining fixtures stopped on the missing legacy swing encoder. Both 56-check cases were repeated successfully after correcting the private codec; no production behavior or assertions were weakened."
  ],
